Feature: SQL Aggregation of Integrated Sales Metrics by Brand, Product, Market, Competitor Flag, Channel, and Transaction Time

  This feature calculates the total integrated_units, integrated_normalized_units, and integrated_dollars for each unique combination of brand_normalized_name, normalized_name, market_normalized_name, competitor_flag, channel_name, and transaction_timestamp from the purgo_playground.bai_sales_agg_obu_customer_datapack_weekly table, applying specific business rules and validation logic.

  Background:
    Given the source table is purgo_playground.bai_sales_agg_obu_customer_datapack_weekly
    And the following columns are used for grouping and aggregation:
      | brand_normalized_name |
      | normalized_name       |
      | market_normalized_name|
      | competitor_flag       |
      | channel_name          |
      | transaction_timestamp |
    And the aggregation columns are:
      | integrated_units           |
      | integrated_normalized_units|
      | integrated_dollars         |
    And the cdl_effective_date column is used for transaction date filtering
    And the br_gpo_flag column is used for GPO flag filtering
    And only rows where market_normalized_name is one of ["trastuzumab-anns", "bevacizumab-awwb", "rituximab market"] are included

  Scenario: Happy path - Valid rows with no KAISER GPO flag and transaction date within 36 months
    Given a row with brand_normalized_name = "kanjinti"
    And br_gpo_flag does not contain "KAISER"
    And market_normalized_name = "trastuzumab-anns"
    And transaction_timestamp is within 36 months prior to cdl_effective_date
    When the SQL script aggregates the row
    Then the integrated_units, integrated_normalized_units, and integrated_dollars are summed as per their values

  Scenario Outline: Error path - Brand is kanjinti, mvasi, or riabni and GPO flag contains KAISER
    Given a row with brand_normalized_name = <brand>
    And br_gpo_flag contains "KAISER"
    And market_normalized_name = <market>
    And transaction_timestamp is within 36 months prior to cdl_effective_date
    When the SQL script aggregates the row
    Then the integrated_units, integrated_normalized_units, and integrated_dollars are treated as zero for this row

    Examples:
      | brand    | market              |
      | kanjinti | trastuzumab-anns    |
      | mvasi    | bevacizumab-awwb    |
      | riabni   | rituximab market    |

  Scenario Outline: Error path - Transaction date outside 36 months window
    Given a row with brand_normalized_name = <brand>
    And br_gpo_flag does not contain "KAISER"
    And market_normalized_name = <market>
    And transaction_timestamp is more than 36 months prior to cdl_effective_date
    When the SQL script aggregates the row
    Then the row is excluded from aggregation

    Examples:
      | brand    | market              |
      | kanjinti | trastuzumab-anns    |
      | mvasi    | bevacizumab-awwb    |
      | riabni   | rituximab market    |
      | other    | trastuzumab-anns    |

  Scenario Outline: Error path - Market not in allowed list
    Given a row with brand_normalized_name = <brand>
    And br_gpo_flag does not contain "KAISER"
    And market_normalized_name = <market>
    And transaction_timestamp is within 36 months prior to cdl_effective_date
    When the SQL script aggregates the row
    Then the row is excluded from aggregation

    Examples:
      | brand    | market           |
      | kanjinti | other-market     |
      | mvasi    | abc-market       |
      | riabni   | xyz-market       |
      | other    | not-in-list      |

  Scenario Outline: Error path - Null or missing key columns
    Given a row with <column> is null
    When the SQL script aggregates the row
    Then the row is excluded from aggregation

    Examples:
      | column                  |
      | brand_normalized_name   |
      | normalized_name         |
      | market_normalized_name  |
      | competitor_flag         |
      | channel_name            |
      | transaction_timestamp   |
      | cdl_effective_date      |

  Scenario Outline: Data-driven aggregation for valid combinations
    Given a row with brand_normalized_name = <brand>
    And normalized_name = <product>
    And market_normalized_name = <market>
    And competitor_flag = <competitor_flag>
    And channel_name = <channel>
    And transaction_timestamp = <transaction_time>
    And br_gpo_flag does not contain "KAISER"
    And transaction_timestamp is within 36 months prior to cdl_effective_date
    And market_normalized_name is in ["trastuzumab-anns", "bevacizumab-awwb", "rituximab market"]
    When the SQL script aggregates the row
    Then the output contains the sum of integrated_units, integrated_normalized_units, and integrated_dollars for the group

    Examples:
      | brand    | product      | market              | competitor_flag | channel      | transaction_time      |
      | kanjinti | KANJINTI     | trastuzumab-anns    | true           | HOSPITAL     | 2023-01-01T00:00:00Z |
      | mvasi    | MVASI        | bevacizumab-awwb    | false          | RETAIL       | 2022-06-15T00:00:00Z |
      | riabni   | RIABNI       | rituximab market    | true           | HOSPITAL     | 2021-12-01T00:00:00Z |
      | other    | OTHERPROD    | trastuzumab-anns    | false          | RETAIL       | 2023-05-10T00:00:00Z |

  Scenario: Validation - Output format and destination
    Given the aggregation is complete
    When the SQL script produces results
    Then the output contains columns:
      | brand_normalized_name      |
      | normalized_name            |
      | market_normalized_name     |
      | competitor_flag            |
      | channel_name               |
      | transaction_timestamp      |
      | total_integrated_units     |
      | total_integrated_normalized_units |
      | total_integrated_dollars  |
    And the output is written to the specified destination (table, view, or file) as per requirements

  Scenario Outline: Error path - Invalid cdl_effective_date format
    Given a row with cdl_effective_date in an invalid format
    When the SQL script processes the row
    Then the row is excluded from aggregation
    And an error message "Invalid cdl_effective_date format" is logged

    Examples:
      | cdl_effective_date |
      | "2023/01/01"       |
      | "01-01-2023"       |
      | "not-a-date"       |
      | null               |

  Scenario: Validation - Handling of nulls in aggregation columns
    Given a row with null values in integrated_units, integrated_normalized_units, or integrated_dollars
    When the SQL script aggregates the row
    Then null values are treated as zero in the sum

  Scenario Outline: Error path - GPO flag filter applies only to bai_sales_agg_obu_customer_datapack_weekly
    Given a row from purgo_playground.bai_sales_agg_obu_customer_datapack_weekly
    And brand_normalized_name is <brand>
    And br_gpo_flag contains "KAISER"
    When the SQL script aggregates the row
    Then integrated_units, integrated_normalized_units, and integrated_dollars are treated as zero

    Examples:
      | brand    |
      | kanjinti |
      | mvasi    |
      | riabni   |

  Scenario Outline: Error path - GPO flag filter does not apply to other tables
    Given a row from a table other than purgo_playground.bai_sales_agg_obu_customer_datapack_weekly
    And brand_normalized_name is <brand>
    And br_gpo_flag contains "KAISER"
    When the SQL script aggregates the row
    Then integrated_units, integrated_normalized_units, and integrated_dollars are not zeroed out

    Examples:
      | brand    |
      | kanjinti |
      | mvasi    |
      | riabni   |
